# Trivy risk acceptances – each entry needs a reason and an expiry date (exp:YYYY-MM-DD).
# After the expiry date Trivy reports the CVE again, forcing a re-review.
# See docs/Issues.md #8.

# Spring Framework 6.2.x (spring-webmvc): no fixed 6.2.x release; fix only in 7.0.x (Spring Boot 4).
# Not exploitable here: VoltCart does not use XsltView or any XSLT view rendering.
# Plan: upgrade to Spring Boot 4 / Spring Framework 7.
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2027-02-28

# Spring Framework 6.2.x (spring-webmvc / spring-webflux): no fixed 6.2.x release; fix only in 7.0.x.
# Not exploitable here: VoltCart does not use Server-Sent Events with view rendering
# (all endpoints return JSON from @RestController).
# Plan: upgrade to Spring Boot 4 / Spring Framework 7.
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2027-02-28

# Spring Framework 6.2.x (spring-webflux, api-gateway): header-predicate bypass in WebFlux *functional
# endpoints*; no fixed 6.2.x release, fix only in 7.0.x.
# Not exploitable here: the gateway defines no functional endpoints (no RouterFunction /
# RequestPredicates / HandlerFunction); routing uses Spring Cloud Gateway's RouteLocator path predicates.
# Accepted by the project owner on 2026-11-21. Plan: upgrade to Spring Boot 4 / Spring Framework 7.
CVE-2026-47892 exp:2027-02-28

# nginx 1.30.6 (frontend base image nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:1.30.6-alpine): fixed in nginx 1.30.7,
# but no nginx-unprivileged image with 1.30.7 was published yet (checked 2026-11-21).
# Not exploitable here: VoltCart's nginx serves plain HTTP/1.1 on port 8080 only – no http2, no
# http3/quic, no ssl, no mail module (TLS/HTTP2 to the internet are handled by the AWS load balancer).
# Accepted by the project owner on 2026-11-21 with a SHORT expiry. Plan: bump to the 1.30.7 image.
CVE-2026-113425 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-121810 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-123007 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-123633 exp:2026-12-31
